.TH PATH_QUOTE_SPACES 3
.SH NAME
path_quote_spaces \- wrap a path in quotes if it contains spaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_quote_spaces(stralloc* " sa ", const char* " s ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_quote_spaces
checks if the null-terminated string
.I s
contains any space characters. If spaces are found, the function wraps the string in double quotes ('"') and stores the result in the
.B stralloc
structure pointed to by
.IR sa .
If no spaces are present, the string is copied to
.I sa
as-is.
.PP
The implementation accounts for UTF-8 encoded characters. The resulting buffer in
.I sa
is null-terminated.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B 1
Spaces were found and the path was quoted.
.TP
.B 0
No spaces were found and the path was copied without quotes.
.TP
.B -1
An error occurred, such as an invalid UTF-8 sequence.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stralloc (3)